{"id":"ENES138","title":"Exploring Engineering Design Through Dialogue","department":"Engineering Science","level":"Undergrad","credits":"1","description":"Restriction: Must be a student in the A. James Clark School of Engineering or in the Global Engineering Leadership minor. Credit only granted for: ENES338K, CHSE338K, or ENES138. Formerly: ENES338K.\n\nThrough deliberate reflections on the past and current patterns of exclusion and inclusion within engineering, you will develop skills for engaging in equitable and inclusive processes and practices that can transform your collaborations and approach to engineering and the design process. This course engages students, from multiple social identity groups, in facilitated dialogue that focus on the tensions, similarities, and differences of experience that exist within, between, and/or across groups.","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"202308","sections":4,"seats":64,"openSeats":8,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Le-Marie Thompson","Paige Smith","Lauren Ruszczyk","Matthew Scassero","Aileen Hentz","Adam Klager","Aralia Ramirez"],"removed":false},{"term":"202401","sections":2,"seats":64,"openSeats":4,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Le-Marie Thompson","Edward Eisenstein","Suzanne Ashour-Bailey","Matt Scassero","LaShanna Young","Timothy Farrell","Alexis Herbert","Adam Klager"],"removed":false},{"term":"202408","sections":2,"seats":64,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Le-Marie Thompson","Edward Eisenstein","Paige Smith","Matt Scassero","LaShanna Young","Daniel Serrano","Erin Wessell","Freddie Dufresne"],"removed":false},{"term":"202501","sections":2,"seats":64,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Kelly McNulty","Aralia Ramirez","Brian Dillehay","David Tomblin","Erin Wessell","LaShanna Young","Abby Shantzis","Shannon Buenaflor","Le-Marie Thompson","Edward Eisenstein"],"removed":false},{"term":"202508","sections":2,"seats":64,"openSeats":0,"waitl